{"title": "fix(branch-placement): `resolveBranch` answers only with a real branch", "body": "Closes #808. Part of #803, direction (2) — the sibling that materialises the PR head branch (#807) is independent of this.

## What changed

`resolveBranch()` (`src/lib/branch-placement.ts`) had three routes and its last one returned whatever git said:

```ts
const { code, stdout } = gitRun("branch", "--format=%(refname:short)", "--points-at=HEAD");
if (code === 0 && stdout) return stdout.split("\n")[0]!;
```

On a detached HEAD, `git branch` prints its own pseudo-entry for HEAD — `(HEAD detached at pull/802/head)` — and `--format` does not suppress it. That string was returned as a branch name and `commitAndPush` handed it straight to `git push -u origin '(HEAD detached at pull/802/head)'`, which answered `fatal: invalid refspec`.

Every route is now verified rather than assumed:

- `isLocalBranch(name)` rejects an empty string, the literal `HEAD`, and any name beginning with `(`, then confirms the rest with `git show-ref --verify --quiet refs/heads/<name>`.
- The `BRANCH` route and the `rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD` route go through it unchanged in intent.
- The `--points-at` route now checks **every line** rather than the first, so it keeps answering for the case it was written for — a detached HEAD that genuinely sits at a **local** branch tip — and rejects the `pr`-run case, a detached HEAD at a fetched pull-request head that no local branch names.
- When nothing resolves it throws a message naming the state, not a symptom: *"This run is on a detached checkout with no local branch, so there is no branch to push: commit_and_push and create_pr cannot publish this run's work. Report the work on the issue instead."*

`commitAndPush` already calls `branchForCommit(REPO)` before `git add -A` and `git commit`; that order and property are kept, so on a run with no resolvable branch the tool fails before creating a commit and the work stays in the working tree where the agent can report it. `create_pr` calls `resolveBranch()` too and gets the same message. `syncBranch`'s `git branch --show-current` refusal is untouched.

## Verification

`bun run typecheck`, `bun run synth`, `bun run test` (972 pass / 0 fail), `bun run test:e2e` (3 pass, 5 skip, 0 fail), `bun run src/scripts/scan_secrets.ts` — all run with `ATOMATON_RUN_TYPE`, `ISSUE_NUMBER` and `ATOMATON_MACHINERY_ROOT` unset, per `hermeticEnv()`'s note. (`scan_secrets` warns it could not resolve the latest gitleaks release, so it scanned nothing; that is upstream, not this change.)

Tests, and each was checked against the previous implementation:

- `src/lib/lib.test.ts` — a new `branch-placement.ts resolveBranch` block against **real repositories**, since the pseudo-entry is git's output and a faked git would only assert the test's own idea of it:
  - `BRANCH` naming a real branch is the answer;
  - on a real branch, `HEAD` names it;
  - a detached HEAD at a local branch tip still answers with that branch, with the pseudo-entry visible as the first line and skipped;
  - the reported failure reproduced — `refs/remotes/pull/802/head` checked out detached, `main` deleted so `git branch --points-at HEAD` prints exactly `(HEAD detached at pull/802/head)` — asserting that value is **not** returned and the error names the state and contains no `refspec`;
  - a `BRANCH` value that is not a local branch falls through to git;
  - no branch at all refuses rather than returning an empty string.
- `src/atomaton-runtime/tools/mcp/mcp.test.ts` — against `makeRemoteBranchFixture()`'s real remote and worktree:
  - `commit_and_push` on a detached HEAD fails with that message and **makes no commit**: `git rev-parse HEAD` is unchanged and `git status --porcelain` still shows the change;
  - `create_pr` on the same worktree fails with the same class of message;
  - an `issue` run still creates its branch at the first commit and opens its pull request from that branch (`gh pr create` handed `atomaton/issue-1`), which is the flow criterion 6 asks to keep working.

Reverting only `resolveBranch()` to its previous body makes the four new `lib.test.ts` cases and both detached-HEAD MCP cases fail with the real symptom (`fatal: invalid refspec '(HEAD detached at 9b2e152)'` and `Remote branch '(HEAD detached at 9b2e152)' does not exist`).

`src/lib/**` is a governed path, so this needs a person at the merge.
", "reviewer": "reviewer"}

